// [over.match.viable] gate for the VALUE-intrinsic contract — a method call
// passing a class object where only a `value &` parameter exists is
// ILL-FORMED, not the arity pick. Pre-fix, reselect_method_overload kept
// the by-name candidate on the scored miss in evaluated contexts and the
// call compiled passing the raw object pointer as a madc::value* (the
// channel readline(value&)-took-std::string* type confusion; g++/clang
// reject the analogous call). ddARRAY's conversion surface is closed by
// construction, so this miss is provable; the GENERAL class-vs-class
// diagnostic is a recorded follow-up (needs scorer conversion modeling).
#include <string>
#include <stdio.h>

struct Sink {
    bool take(value &v) { printf("take value\n"); return true; }
};

int main()
{
    Sink s;
    string line = "hello";
    s.take(line);
    return 0;
}
